        <item>
            <title>0.8.4</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 13:43:24 +1200</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>15</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.8.4</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}.rn{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,"SF Pro Text",sans-serif;color:#1d1d1f;margin:4px 2px}.rn h1{font-size:16px;margin:0 0 10px}.rn h2{font-size:14px;margin:14px 0 6px}.rn ul{margin:6px 0;padding-left:20px}.rn li{margin-bottom:7px}.rn code{font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12px}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.rn{color:#e8e8ed}}</style><div class="rn"><h1>Rein 0.8.4</h1>
<ul>
<li><b>Cast controls in the menu bar.</b> While a video casts, the Rein panel shows a transport: play/pause, a scrubber with elapsed/total time, and the TV volume — no need to open the full window.</li>
<li><b>Your keyboard's play/pause key now controls the cast.</b> Rein registers as the Mac's Now Playing app during a cast, so the ⏯ media key, AirPods taps, and Control Center's transport all drive the Chromecast — including scrubbing from Control Center.</li>
<li>Also in this update (0.8.3): casting sound now works on every TV — Dolby audio converts to AAC automatically, with a per-device "Dolby passthrough" opt-in for soundbar setups.</li>
</ul></div>
]]></description>
